    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "13. Those who do not possess learning, or practise",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "penance or give gifts, or have knowledge, character, virtue",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "or religious merit, roam in the mortal world as beasts in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "a human form, a mere burden to the earth.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "14. Better would it be to wander in company with for-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "esters through the inaccessible regions of mountains than to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "live in the company of fools even in the halls of the Lord",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "of gods.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "15. That renowned learned men whose speech is charming",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "owing to the use of words refined by the S'ástras and whose",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "knowledge is worth being imparted to disciples live in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "poverty in the dominions of a king, bespeaks the stupidity",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "(want of appreciation) of the king. Even without wealth",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "learned men are kings. The jewels are not to blame but the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "wicked lapidaries by whom they are appraised much below",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "their worth.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "16 The secret treasure of knowledge is not destroyed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "even at the end of the world, does not fall into the hands of a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "thief, ever yields some ( indescribable ) happiness, and when",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "given to those that solicit it, increases plentifully. Cast away",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "your pride, ye kings, towards those who have this treasure.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Who can rival them ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "17. Do not despise wise men who have obtained the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "highest good; wealth, worthless as grass, stands not in their",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "way; a lotus-fibre cannot present any obstacle to elephants",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "whose temples have been darkened with a stream of fresh",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "rut.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
